# Overlay example: design-consistency

Drop this file at `<consumer>/.claude/skills/design-consistency/SKILL.md.local`.
It is APPENDED to the plugin's SKILL.md at runtime (extend-only — never replaces plugin behavior).

The plugin's generic skill covers the reuse-before-invent framework. This overlay names your project's actual design system so the grep-first rule has concrete targets.

---

## <product> design system

### Themed primitives (use over raw HTML)

- **`<ThemedInput />`** — never raw `<input>`
- **`<ThemedSelect />`** — never raw `<select>`
- **`<Button />` (gradient variant)** — primary CTAs
- (List every themed wrapper your project has)

### Design tokens (verbatim — don't drift)

```
page wrapper:   bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 via-purple-900 to-slate-900 pt-20 pb-10
container:      max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4    (or max-w-6xl for admin)
card surface:   bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/20 rounded-xl
primary CTA:    bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 to-pink-600 hover:from-purple-700 hover:to-pink-700
tooltip:        bg-gray-900/95 backdrop-blur-sm border-white/20 text-white
nav clearance:  pt-20  (HARD rule per .claude/rules/ui-design.md)
```

### Domain component directories (grep these first)

- `components/<domain1>/` — what it owns
- `components/<domain2>/` — what it owns
- `components/admin/` — admin tables, etc.

### Stock primitives location

`components/ui/` — shadcn (or equivalent) primitives. `ls` here before inventing.

### Icon library

`lucide-react` — pick names consistent with adjacent pages.

### Toast / inline-feedback helper

`useToast()` from `components/ui/use-toast.tsx`. Standard variants (default, destructive).
